<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mumadona Dias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 968</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mumadona Dias was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galician-portuguese">Galician-Portuguese</a> noblewoman who governed the County of Portugal in the mid-10th century after the death of her husband, Count Hermenegildo Gonçalves. She founded a monastery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guimaraes">Guimarães</a> and built a castle to protect it from Norse and Muslim raiders, the origin of Guimarães Castle. She was one of the greatest landholders of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mumadona-dias.jpg" alt="Mumadona Dias" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tm; estátua por Álvaro Brée · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Est%C3%A1tua_a_Mumadona_Dias_no_Largo_da_Mumadona_04.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
